    "done_when": "Subscription lanes must reach Jev with their last reading and its age, never as null when a reading exists.\n\nMeasured 2026-10-06 from the ledger rows since 2026-10-04T13:00Z: 1,953 codex candidates were offered to the picker. 1,449 had burn_multiple null, and 1,422 of those had budget_reason \"recorded account-window reading is stale\". reckon/crew/picker/snapshot.py budget_view turns a reading past its staleness horizon into a null burn and pace. Jev's question template already says to weigh \"budget source, age and stale flag\", so dropping the figure contradicts the picker's own design, and it blinds Jev exactly when codex has been idle.\n\n1. The dispatch-path picker carries a stale reading into the candidate with its utilisation, burn_multiple, pace_allowance, days_to_reset, observed age and stale: true, instead of nulling it. Only a genuinely absent reading stays null with its budget_reason. Add no numeric age cut-off in code; Jev weighs the age. If the candidate schema has no age field, add one, and say so.\n2. Tests in tests/test_stale_reading_reaches_jev.py:\n   - a stale published or recorded reading yields a candidate with non-null figures, its age and stale true;\n   - an absent reading still yields nulls and the named reason;\n   - a fresh reading is unchanged.\n   Tests must never call a live provider.\n3. Evidence in docs/evidence/fragments/one-typesafe-model-picker/stale-reading-reaches-jev.html: a replay of the picker's candidate build over a fixture with a two-hour-old codex reading, before and after, and one live reckon crew pick showing a codex candidate with burn, pace and age.\n\nDo not edit reckon/crew/paid_lanes.py, which another run claims; the publisher refetch is a separate node.\n\nGate: tests/test_picker*.py, tests/test_budget*.py, tests/test_paid_lanes_codex_window.py and the new test file. Run them with the main checkout's .venv/bin/python -m pytest -p no:cacheprovider -n 8 in the FOREGROUND, with one log for base and one for head under the run directory, each ending in an EXIT line, judged by delta.",
